Sebastian Bleasdale wrote:
> Another possibility would be making alter creation a priest-only ability.
> This could be accomplished by (say) the priest dropping a loadstone
> somewhere and praying on top of it, and with sufficiently high alignment,
> etc.

For increased difficulty/complexity, the loadstone could be required to 
be of the same "alignment" as the priest (blesed if lawful, uncursed if 
neutral, cursed if chaotic). This would make it an interesting exercise 
for a chaotic priest to set up an altar in the preferred spot (would 
polymorphing yourself into an armless monster do the trick?). As the 
original poster suggested, I would also suggest the requirement of at 
least one "additional item", perhaps the corpse of a sufficiently 
powerful cross-aligned monster, possibly also "re-aligned" by 
blessing/uncursing/cursing. The priest should then "offer" instead of 
"pray" on top of it.

There would have to be a rumor about it, otherwise new players would 
never catch on. Therefore the explanation cannot be too long (unless you 
make it a "major" Oracle consultation). Why not make a rumor at once 
(put it in the "false rumors" lot at first): "It is said that a chaotic 
priest can offer a cursed corpse on a cursed loadstone." (the 
cross-alignment goes without saynig)

